{"id":"neubrutalism","title":"Neubrutalism","url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Neubrutalism","rev":236777,"fetched":"2026-10-16","lead":[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"b","c":["Neubrutalism"]}," (also spelt ",{"t":"b","c":["Neo Brutalism"]},", and alternatively referred to as ",{"t":"b","c":["Neo Memphis"]},") is a design aesthetic that focuses on breaking the traditional conventions of design by using unconventional visual elements, such as contrasting color palettes and grotesque typefaces."]}],"sections":[{"title":"History","id":"history","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"b","c":["Neubrutalism"]},"'s namesake originates from the architectural movement ",{"t":"a","c":["Brutalism"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Brutalism"},", which utilized unpainted concrete and geometric designs, favoring functionality over conventional aesthetic standards; ",{"t":"a","c":["Brutalism"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Brutalism"}," was minimalist, utilitarian, monochrome in nature. Although ",{"t":"a","c":["Brutalism"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Brutalism"}," and ",{"t":"b","c":["Neubrutalism"]}," are very different visually, they both share the core value of breaking the conventions of design and create visuals in their most basic shapes and forms."]},{"t":"p","c":["Microsoft Windows 1.0 (1985) featured most of ",{"t":"b","c":["Neubrutalism'"]},"s key visual motifs listed below, including hard 45º angled shadows in built-in apps such as Reversi and Calculator, a pseudo-3D view of the reversi board, dark outlines, contrasting colors in menus/scrollbars/backgrounds, uppercase lettering in the MS-DOS Executive app, a typeface that would be considered rather unusual in most contexts, quite geometric blocks, and the ability to randomly rearrange the layout of windows."]},{"t":"p","c":["Other early examples of the ",{"t":"b","c":["Neubrutalist"]}," movement can be traced as back to the Early/Mid-2010s, but the aesthetic that is commonly recognized as ",{"t":"b","c":["Neubrutalism"]}," would not form until the Late-2010s/Early-2020s, when it started to become more widespread. Around 2022-2023, ",{"t":"b","c":["Neubrutalism"]}," became mainstream within UI/UX and graphic design, with websites, apps, and advertisement adopting the aesthetic."]}]},{"title":"Visuals","id":"visuals","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"b","c":["Neubrutalism"]},"'s visuals focus on defying the traditional principles of design. This is a contrast to ",{"t":"a","c":["Flat Design"],"id":"flat-design"},", which focuses on conforming to the traditional conventions of design. However, ",{"t":"b","c":["Neubrutalism"]}," and ",{"t":"a","c":["Flat Design"],"id":"flat-design"}," both share the common purpose of easing accessibility and improving functionality."]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"b","c":["Neubrutalism'"]},"s key visual motifs include:"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Geometric blocks"]},{"c":["Contrasting and off-putting color palettes"]},{"c":["Unusual and grotesque typography"]},{"c":["Stretched typefaces"]},{"c":["Uppercase lettering"]},{"c":["Hard 45º angled shadows"]},{"c":["Dark outlines"]},{"c":["Oversized UI/UX"]},{"c":["Illustrations and static animations"]},{"c":["Pseudo-3D objects"]},{"c":["The lack of gradients or other visual effects"]},{"c":["Random or inconsistent layout"]},{"c":["1930's-style cartoon characters"]},{"c":["Realistic outline illustrations, empty and/or unshaded"]}]},{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"b","c":["Neubrutalism"]}," is also heavily driven by 1990s and Early-2000s nostalgia, especially driven by ",{"t":"a","c":["Memphis Design"],"id":"memphis-design"}," and ",{"t":"a","c":["Webcore"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Webcore"},", which both share visual motifs with ",{"t":"b","c":["Neubrutalism"]}," such as geometric shapes, zig-zagged lines, graph paper grids, computer windows/tabs and icons, and ",{"t":"a","c":["Y2K Futurism"],"id":"y2k-futurism"}," inspired imagery."]}]},{"title":"Websites","id":"websites","blocks":[{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["Gumroad"],"href":"https://gumroad.com/"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["Mozilla: The Super-Official Family Tech Agreement"],"href":"https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/firefox/family/"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["Figma"],"href":"https://www.figma.com/"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["Readymag"],"href":"https://readymag.com/readymag/projects-of-the-year-2021/first-page/"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["Pizza Pizza"],"href":"https://pizzapizza.io/"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["Guía de Cirugía Cardíaca"],"href":"https://guiacirugiacardiaca.com/"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["Christou 1910 DAYS"],"href":"https://days.christou1910.com/en/"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["Plus"],"href":"https://cleanwith.plus/"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["Mafanfa"],"href":"https://mafanfa.com/"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["Groupe Castor & Pollux"],"href":"https://groupe.castoretpollux.com/en/"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["Badass35"],"href":"https://www.badass35.com/en/home"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["The Great Lake Michigan"],"href":"https://thegreatlake.fun/"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["Budapest Park"],"href":"https://www.budapestpark.hu/en"}]},{"c":[{"t":"a","c":["Google I/O 2024"],"href":"https://io.google/2024/"}]}]}]},{"title":"Gallery","id":"gallery","blocks":[{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/0/0a/Neubrutalistexample.png/revision/latest?cb=20230903051339","w":160,"h":160},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/7/72/638537fcab2f0b1a4eda5f08_neo-brutalism.png/revision/latest?cb=20230903052314","w":160,"h":160},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/c/c5/1f9d5e56-28f1-4756-b32e-4363930446dd-cover.png/revision/latest?cb=20230903052313","w":160,"h":160},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/1/10/Original-c04ab36886c294a1f26ec6ec243807e6.png/revision/latest?cb=20230903052222","w":160,"h":160},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/4/4c/94dcc0401551a650e2d76460f14e6bef.png/revision/latest?cb=